= FatFs

This is a copy of FatFs, a "generic FAT file system module for small embedded
systems", by ChaN. See http://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/00index_e.html.

Please submit bug reports to the http://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/bd/[FatFs
User Forum], not to this repo.

== Tags

This repository continues the https://github.com/abbrev/fatfs[abbrev/fatfs]
mirror of ChaN's release archives and patches. Tags follow the same scheme as
https://github.com/xmosforks/PetitFatFs[xmosforks/PetitFatFs]:

`R<version>`:: The upstream release archive as imported, for example `R0.16`.
`R<version>.post<N>`:: That release with upstream's official patches 1 to N
applied, for example `R0.16.post3`. Each patch is a separate commit titled
`R<version> patch <N>` carrying the upstream description.
`R<version>[.post<N>]+xmos.<M>`:: XMOS source changes on top of either of the
above. None exist at present.

The `.post<N>` and `+xmos.<M>` suffixes borrow the post-release and local
version spellings of PEP 440; the upstream version itself is not PEP 440
compliant. README-only commits are not tagged. Consuming libraries pin one of
these tags.

The mirror originally placed each `R<version>` tag on the last patch of that
release. Those tags were moved to the release imports and `.post<N>` tags were
added when this scheme was adopted, and the earlier `R0.16+xmos.1` tag, which
contained no XMOS changes, was replaced by `R0.16.post3`. The `R0.16` import
has been compared with the official `ff16.zip` (SHA-256
`99f7dc1f7e095356e4a9e3dbe29959090d8b948afe2bbc5441e52fdf4b85449e`) and its
`source` directory is identical. Earlier imports are as made by the mirror and
have not been re-verified.

